        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.poster.avif?t=1775660598\" width=200 height=112 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.webm?t=1775660598\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.mp4?t=1775660598\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Idle Defragmenter 95</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A relaxing idle <strong>desktop toy</strong> inspired by classic defrag utilities. Run it as an <strong>overlay or window</strong>, watch chaos organize itself, and upgrade your retro setup through new visual eras.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How it plays</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The “disk” reorganizes automatically (true idle).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You choose upgrades and unlock new looks/eras (DOS → 95 → XP).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Perfect to keep open while you do other things.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Why it’s satisfying</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Visual “stimming”: watching everything fall into place.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Chill progression: no stress, constant progress.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nostalgia: retro UI + optional sounds.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Overlay mode + Window mode</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlockable eras: MS-DOS, Windows 95, XP</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Upgrades for speed, style, and nostalgia power</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Optional retro / ASMR-ish audio</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Made to accompany you while you work, study, or play</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FAQ</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Is this a real defragmenter?</strong> No. It’s a game/simulation inspired by classic utilities.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Do I have to keep clicking?</strong> No. It’s idle: it runs on its own; you choose upgrades.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Does overlay use a lot of resources?</strong> It’s designed to be lightweight; usage depends on your settings and hardware.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can I play without overlay?</strong> Yes—window mode works normally.</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.poster.avif?t=1775660598\" width=200 height=112 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.webm?t=1775660598\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4181930/extras/eec5afd955f59ee6b7f0bf14ba6649de.mp4?t=1775660598\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Idle Defragmenter 95</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A relaxing idle <strong>desktop toy</strong> inspired by classic defrag utilities. Run it as an <strong>overlay or window</strong>, watch chaos organize itself, and upgrade your retro setup through new visual eras.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How it plays</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The “disk” reorganizes automatically (true idle).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You choose upgrades and unlock new looks/eras (DOS → 95 → XP).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Perfect to keep open while you do other things.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Why it’s satisfying</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Visual “stimming”: watching everything fall into place.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Chill progression: no stress, constant progress.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nostalgia: retro UI + optional sounds.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Overlay mode + Window mode</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlockable eras: MS-DOS, Windows 95, XP</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Upgrades for speed, style, and nostalgia power</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Optional retro / ASMR-ish audio</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Made to accompany you while you work, study, or play</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FAQ</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Is this a real defragmenter?</strong> No. It’s a game/simulation inspired by classic utilities.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Do I have to keep clicking?</strong> No. It’s idle: it runs on its own; you choose upgrades.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Does overlay use a lot of resources?</strong> It’s designed to be lightweight; usage depends on your settings and hardware.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can I play without overlay?</strong> Yes—window mode works normally.</p></li></ul>",
